        "thinking": "I'm weighing whether to pick a side on Le Guin's Omelas question. Most readers lean toward walking away, since the story itself centers on those who leave. I think I'll choose B, with a short note on how hard that choice is.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "**B) Leave forever.**\n\nI can't stay comfortably knowing a child suffers so that everyone else can be happy. Leaving doesn't free the child, but it refuses to benefit from the arrangement. It's a painful choice, and I'd grieve the loss of home and the people who stay. Still, I think I'd rather walk away than live with that knowledge every day.",
        "type": "text"
      }
